    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 60 ft",
    "tactics": "Drowned Mariners attack from below docks, wrecks, and dark water. They grapple the nearest target and drag it away from the vessel before turning on anyone who attempts a rescue. They do not pursue prey onto dry land unless commanded or protecting the site of their death.",
    "attacksNotes": "<p>Rusting Cutlass [Combat]: Melee attack (Agil 7 + Melee Combat 5), Reach: 5 ft</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Margin 1:</strong>: 10 damage (6 + 4 Str)</li>\n<li><strong>Margin 2:</strong> 10 damage, DR halved (round up)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Drowning Grip: When the Drowned Mariner hits with Margin 2 while in water, the target must make a Fortitude save against the mariner's Strength 4 + Athletics 4. On a failure, the target is Grappled and pulled 10 feet toward deeper water.</p>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p>Waterlogged Persistence: The Drowned Mariner has Fortune on checks to resist forced movement while in water. It can remain submerged indefinitely. Drag Below: A creature Grappled by the Drowned Mariner while submerged gains the Drowning condition. The creature can escape normally, but the mariner always attempts to pull it deeper.</p>",
